    NH 3.1 runs fine for me on a 286, using MS-DOS 5 and Smartdrive as
a big disk cache.  Most of the slowness you see running the game in
low memory is due to the rather astounding amount of code swapping it
seems to do - when you set up the disk cache, this all goes away.
    It's still slow when going up or down levels, or loading or
saving a game, but normal game play is perfectly acceptable.  I
think a 2MB cache would probably be sufficient to get the job
done.

